. December accounts for 9% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 14% of all its works contracts. Contract [1], for 39,669.42 euros, was awarded in December 2025. Contract [2], for 39,400 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The fact that many contracts are just under the limit does not mean that any of them were improperly awarded. It could reflect standard market pricing, budget constraints, or the need for multiple smaller contracts to meet specific requirements.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see what was purchased and the specific reason for the amount. Also, review contract [2] to confirm if the same service or product was bought in another contract. Look for patterns in the dates and awardees to determine if multiple contracts were used for the same need.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["IFqkpvvkiTc%2B1TMyIiZmzw%3D%3D","D9M312%2F47jyGCFcHcNGIlQ%3D%3D","C1ZvT0aeSVZrhBlEHQFSKA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}